  "fields": {
   "meta-description": "What a thank you page is, four examples by use case, and templates to build in minutes, for WooCommerce, Shopify, or any form. Free to start.",
   "acrm---key-feature-5-content": "<h3>Works everywhere your form does</h3><p>A custom thank you page for WooCommerce, a Shopify post-purchase page, a WordPress form, or any standalone URL. One build, every surface, one set of submissions in your database.</p>",
   "alpb---how-to-step-6-des": "Connect your domain, set the page to noindex, and point the form, checkout, or booking redirect at the new URL. On Shopify, link it from the order confirmation email, since its own thank you page no longer runs scripts.",
   "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Thank You Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a thank you page?\", \"a\": \"A thank you page is a dedicated page a visitor lands on after they convert: a form submission, a purchase, a booking, or a signup. It confirms the action, sets expectations for what comes next, and offers one relevant next step. Because it has its own URL, a thank you page can be tracked as a conversion and used as a retargeting source, which an inline confirmation message cannot.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a thank you page say?\", \"a\": \"Confirm the action succeeded, say what happens next and when, and give one clear next step. Add the promised file or link, and a small piece of social proof if it fits. The best thank you page examples pick one next step rather than crowding the page with options.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a thank you page and a confirmation message?\", \"a\": \"A confirmation message is a line of text shown in place. A thank you page is a full URL, so it can be tracked as a conversion goal, targeted with a retargeting pixel, and used to move the visitor to a next step. The difference is measured in the actions you recover from people who already said yes once.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do I need a thank you page after form submission?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if you want to measure the conversion, retarget the visitor, or trigger a follow-up. A tracked thank you page after form submission turns a completed form into a retargeting audience and a next-step opportunity, which a simple inline message cannot do.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a thank you page for free?\", \"a\": \"Describe the action the page follows and the next step you want, and Emergent's <a href=\\\"https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder\\\">AI landing page builder</a> generates the thank you page, wires it to your form backend, and publishes it on your domain. The free tier covers building and publishing a page with a live URL.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I build a custom thank you page for WooCommerce?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Describe what should appear after checkout in WooCommerce, connect the store, and Emergent generates a custom thank you page for WooCommerce that replaces the default confirmation. Order details, a related product, a discount code, or a review request can all sit on the same page.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I create a custom Shopify thank you page?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as a linked page rather than a redirect, because Shopify no longer runs custom scripts on its own thank you page. Link an Emergent post-purchase page from the order confirmation email, with the order, a related product, and a next-order code.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I add a thank you page to a WordPress form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Redirect the form to a thank you page URL and Emergent handles the rest. Works with Contact Form 7, WPForms, Gravity Forms, and any WordPress form that supports a redirect on submit.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are there thank you page templates?\", \"a\": \"Every use case on this page is a thank you page template you can adapt: lead magnet, ecommerce order, webinar or event, contact and booking. Start from the closest one, describe what to change, and publish.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best thank you page examples?\", \"a\": \"The best examples share five things: a plain confirmation, what happens next, one next step, the promised delivery, and light social proof. The four use cases on this page apply them to a lead magnet, an order, a webinar, and a contact form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I track conversions on a thank you page?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Because a thank you page is a real URL, an analytics event and a conversion pixel can be fired on load, which turns the page into a measurable goal and a retargeting source. Emergent injects the pixel and the event on publish.\"}, {\"q\": \"What SEO meta tags should a thank you page have?\", \"a\": \"A thank you page is almost always noindex, so the meta title and description are for humans in browser tabs and share cards. Give it a clear title, a short description, and an OG image; keep it out of the sitemap.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I A/B test a thank you page?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Generate a second variant of the CTA, the hero copy, or the whole page with a prompt, publish both, and compare conversion on the next step by traffic source.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where do the submissions from my thank you page go?\", \"a\": \"Into a database in your Emergent project, and to any tool you connect through a prompt: HubSpot, Mailchimp, Klaviyo, Slack, Google Sheets, or a webhook. Not into a vendor lock-in you have to export from.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
   "awb---mockup-data": "<p id=\"\">window.awbMockup = { leadMagnet: \"Build a lead magnet thank you page shown after form submission that confirms the ebook download with an instant link, sets a two-minute inbox expectation, offers a demo booking as the single next step, and saves the lead with UTMs to a database.\", ecommerceOrder: \"Build a custom thank you page for a Shopify store that confirms the order and delivery timing, offers one related product based on the item purchased, and saves the order to a database with the source of the visit attached.\", webinarEvent: \"Build a webinar thank you page that confirms the registration, offers an add-to-calendar link, shows the reminder schedule, and saves the registration with source and campaign to a database that feeds my email tool.\", contactBooking: \"Build a thank you page after a contact form submission that confirms receipt, names a 24-hour response window, offers a Calendly embed as an alternative, and posts the inquiry to Slack and HubSpot as a new deal.\" };</p>"
  }
 },
 "form": {
  "collection_id": "6aaaaa02995bb2f9f4d6a36c",
  "item_id": "6ab505a8d621dc692561a85a",
  "fields": {
   "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Creator Application Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a creator application?\", \"a\": \"A creator application is the form creators fill in to join a brand's creator, ambassador, affiliate, or UGC program. It collects who they are, where they post, how big and engaged their audience is, and samples of their work, so the brand can decide who to accept.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a creator application form ask?\", \"a\": \"Name and email, social handles per platform, follower count and engagement rate, niche, audience location, content samples or a media kit, rates for paid programs, and a short answer on why they want to work with you. Keep it to around ten fields; every extra question costs completions.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a creator application form?\", \"a\": \"Describe your program in plain English: who can apply, which platforms matter, and how you judge fit. Emergent's <a href=\\\"https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder\\\">AI form builder</a> generates the form, the scoring, and the database, and you refine it by prompting.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I screen creators automatically?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Each application can be scored on follower range, engagement, niche, and region the moment it arrives. Creators who meet your bar go to an approve queue, and the rest can get a waitlist or decline email automatically.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can creators upload content samples and media kits?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The form accepts portfolio links, video samples, and PDF media kits, and each file is stored with the application so reviewers see the work next to the numbers.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where do the applications go?\", \"a\": \"Into a database table inside your Emergent project, with status, score, and source attached. You can filter, export, or build a review dashboard on it, and sync each application to Slack, HubSpot, Airtable, or Google Sheets.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a limit on how many applications I can collect?\", \"a\": \"No. Emergent does not cap responses, so the form keeps collecting through a launch spike. Many form tools cap responses by plan, and some close the form once the cap is reached.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one form handle TikTok, Instagram, and YouTube creators?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Conditional logic shows each platform's questions only when the creator selects it, so a multi-platform creator answers once per channel and a single-platform creator never sees the rest.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a creator application and a brand ambassador application?\", \"a\": \"They overlap. A creator application usually screens for audience and content quality, while a brand ambassador application leans on loyalty and product love, often from existing customers. One form can run both with a branch at the start.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I embed the application form on my website?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Use an inline embed or iframe on Shopify, WordPress, Webflow, or any site, share it as a standalone page on your own domain, or link to it from your bio.\"}, {\"q\": \"What happens after I approve a creator?\", \"a\": \"Whatever you describe. Common next steps are a contract to sign, an affiliate link or discount code, a product seeding request, and a welcome email, all triggered from the approval.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I export the code?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The form, the scoring logic, and the database schema export to your GitHub repository. Keep hosting on Emergent or deploy it anywhere.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
  }
 },
